  "term": "atrophy",
  "definition": "Atrophy is a decrease in the size or working power of a bodily organ or mechanism caused by disuse, injury, or disease. In historical evolutionary usage, it also referred to the shrinking of an organ or tissue because it had become useless or had been replaced in function by another organ.",
